# The burrow tree PAX carries as /bin/ssh and /bin/burrow-keygen (px104;
# tools/mkburrow builds it, tools/install-burrow installs it).
#
# burrow is an ssh client in wolf (wolffe-lang/burrow, the burrow track):
# OpenSSH-compatible for the profile it speaks (curve25519-sha256,
# ssh-ed25519 host and user keys, chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com, strict
# kex), strict known_hosts checking, publickey login with an unencrypted
# Ed25519 key in OpenSSH's format, one command a session with GIT_PROTOCOL
# by SendEnv: the ssh den's ssh:// and scp-like remotes start. Its clean
# room is the SSH RFCs and OpenSSH's PROTOCOL notes (burrow's README); PAX
# reads no more of its tree than building it needs.
#
# burrow 7aa182f (2026-11-11): burrow#26 (bw07), a session's program starts
# with every signal at its default whatever burrowd was started with (before
# it, a burrowd started with SIGINT and SIGQUIT ignored passed that to every
# program over ssh); and burrow#24 (bw06, ab34042), a terminal for burrowd's
# sessions: a `pty-req` granted (`no-pty` and `restrict` keys, and
# `PermitTTY no`, refuse it by name), the session's program the leader of a
# session of its own with the pty's slave its controlling terminal and its
# group the foreground, the client's window changes applied, and a command
# with no pty in a session of its own with no controlling terminal (so
# `/dev/tty` does not open and a bare `sudo` says so instead of stopping on
# the console). Before them, 16858a5: B5's burrowd (burrow#11), password
# authentication against /etc/shadow (burrow#12), the shell with no pty
# (burrow#15), one packet a session's turn (burrow#16), a process group per
# program (burrow#19) and SetEnv in burrowd_config (burrow#23, pax#334).
# Pinned in its own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf 0.2.39 / lupin 0.1.61 /
# wolf-std 77cf3210. tools/mkburrow builds it with THAT toolchain, through
# burrow's own tools/build --static, in two checkouts, refusing two
# digests, and installs all three programs: /bin/ssh, /bin/burrow-keygen and
# /bin/burrowd; it holds its two checkouts to each other, not to a recorded
# digest (the static binary depends on the libc.a it links).
BURROW_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/burrow
BURROW_REV=7aa182f8a8c34137dce5162881496143edb3b090
